-- title:
--   Deuring correspondence: equal idèle classes iff isomorphic curves
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose points killed by $q'$ are zero. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the condition that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated, spanning $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal among such submodules, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}$ of the $\kappa$-points of $X_0$ generated by the rationally represented homomorphisms into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, with range exactly $\Lambda$. Let $x,y$ be units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$. Let $W$, $W'$ be elliptic Weierstrass curves over $\kappa$ and $\chi$, $\chi'$ nonzero additive maps from the points of $X_0$ to those of $W$, resp. $W'$, each either zero or given off a finite exceptional set by fixed rational functions, and let $d,d'$ be units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta$ carries the set of endomorphisms of $X_0$ of the form $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho$ a rationally represented homomorphism $W\to X_0$ onto the conjugate $\overline{d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda})}$, where $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}$ denotes the elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ landing in the left translate by $x$ of the adelic box of $\Lambda$, and similarly for $\chi'$, $d'$, $y$. Then $x$ and $y$ have the same class in the double coset space of units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ by the diagonal image of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ on one side and the stabiliser of the adelic box of $\Lambda$ on the other if and only if there is a variable change $\gamma$ over $\kappa$ with $\gamma\cdot W=W'$.
--
--   This is the well-definedness and injectivity, in the form needed here, of Deuring's map sending a supersingular elliptic curve isogenous to $X_0$ to the class of the kernel ideal of an isogeny $X_0\to W$ among right ideal classes of the maximal order $\Lambda$. It is used in the construction of the bijection between the class set attached to $\Lambda$ and the set of supersingular points entering the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the relevant moduli.
